- var ASRs = ['health', 'care', 'disability']

mixin percentASR(i)
    if ASRs.includes(s[i][0])
        if hasSaid('ASR')
            | proportion
        else 
            | age-standardised proportion
            recordSaid('ASR')
    else
        | percentage

mixin agestandard(i)
    if (!hasSaid('agestandard'))
        - recordSaid('agestandard')
        if (s[i][0] == 'health')
            p
                | Age-standardised proportions
                - recordSaid('ASR')
                | are used throughout this section. They enable comparisons between populations over time and across geographies, as they account for differences in the population size and age structure.
            //- p 
                | Rates are standardised to control for differences in the age structure of the population, which can impact the local population's health. Non-standardised data are available in
                a our datasets
                | .
        if (s[i][0] == 'care')
            p
                | Age-standardised proportions
                - recordSaid('ASR')
                | are used throughout this section. They enable comparisons between populations over time and across geographies, as they account for differences in the population size and age structure.
            //- p 
                | Rates are standardised to control for differences in the age structure of the population, which can impact the local population's provision of unpaid care. Non-standardised data are available in
                a our datasets
                | .
        if (s[i][0] == 'disability')
            p
                if hasSaid('ASR')
                | Age-standardised proportions
                - recordSaid('ASR')
                | are used throughout this section. They enable comparisons between populations over time and across geographies, as they account for differences in the population size and age structure.
            //- p 
                | Rates are standardised to control for differences in the age structure of the population, which can impact the local population's disability rates. Non-standardised data are available in
                a our datasets
                | .


mixin disclaimers(i)
    - console.log("disclaimers")
    //-disclaimers
    if (s[i][0] == 'economic' )
        p 
            | Census 2021 took place during the coronavirus (COVID-19) pandemic, a period of rapid and unparalleled change; the national lockdown, associated guidance and furlough measures will have affected the labour market and our ability to measure it.
    if (s[i][0] == 'marital')
        p These figures include same-sex marriages and opposite-sex civil partnerships in 2021, neither of which were legally recognised in England and Wales in 2011. Same-sex marriages have been legally recognised in England and Wales since 2014 and opposite-sex civil partnerships have been recognised since 2019.
    if (s[i][0] == 'hours')
        p Working hours may have been affected by the coronavirus (COVID-19) pandemic.
    if (s[i][0] == 'national')
        if (place.name == 'Cornwall' )
            p 
                | The 
                a(href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/datasets/TS028/editions/2021/versions/1") National Identity (detailed) 
                a 
                | dataset provides more information on the number of people who identified as Cornish.
            p 
                | The percentage of people in Cornwall who selected a "Cornish" only identity increased from #[+value(0.099, {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})] in 2011 to #[+value(0.14, {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})] in 2021. A further #[+value(0.016, {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})] selected "Cornish" in combination with a "British" identity in 2021, an increase from #[+value(0.010, {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})] in 2011. 
            P In the chart below, people who selected Cornish with any other combination of UK identities were included in "Any other combination of only UK identities".
        p
            | In Census 2021, “British” was moved to the top response option and this may have influenced how people described their national identity. For further information, please see our 
            a(href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/culturalidentity/ethnicity/methodologies/ethnicgroupnationalidentitylanguageandreligionqualityinformationforcensus2021#:~:text=Other%20ethnic%20group%22-,National%20identity,Ordering%20of%20identity") 
                | quality report
            | . 
            //- While the increase in number of usual residents describing their national identity as "British" and the fall in the number describing their national identity as "English" may partly reflect true change, it is most likely to be a result of the changes to the question structure where "British" became the top response option in 2021 for England only.
    if (s[i][0] == 'health')
        p 
            | Census 2021 was conducted during the coronavirus (COVID-19) pandemic. This may have influenced how people perceived and rated their health, and therefore may have affected how people chose to respond.
    if (s[i][0] == 'care')
        p 
            | Census 2021 was undertaken during the coronavirus (COVID-19) pandemic. This may have influenced how people perceived and managed their provision of unpaid care, and therefore may have affected how people chose to respond.
        p 
            | Caution should be taken when making comparisons between 2011 and 2021 because of changes in question wording and response options.
    if (s[i][0] == 'disability')
        p 
            | Census 2021 was undertaken during the coronavirus (COVID-19) pandemic. This may have influenced how people perceived their health status and activity limitations, and therefore may have affected how people chose to respond.
        p 
            | Caution should be taken when making comparisons between 2011 and 2021 because of changes in question wording and response options.
mixin ordi(x)
    if (x!=1)
        | #[+value(parseInt(Math.abs(x)), {'ORDINAL_TEXTUAL':true})]

mixin regional 
    if (parent=="Wales")
        | Welsh
    else
        | regional

mixin region
    if (parent=="Wales")
        | Wales
    else if (parent=="London")
        | Greater London
    else
        | the region

mixin ppoint
    | percentage points
    //- if !hasSaid('PP')
    //-     | percentage points (pp)
    //-     recordSaid('PP')
    //- else
    //-     | pp


mixin nearbyname
    | nearby #[+placeLink(near.name)]

mixin val(x)
    - var sig = parseFloat(x.toPrecision(2))
    synz
        syn
            | around
        syn
            if (x>sig)
                | just over 
            else if (x<sig)
                | just under 
        syn
            | around
        syn
            if (x>sig)
                | just over 
            else if (x<sig)
                | just under
        syn 
            | 
    | #[+value(sig)]

mixin sentopening 
    | between the last two censuses (held in 2011 and 2021)

mixin placeLink(place_name)
    if hasSaid(place_name)
        | !{place_name}
    else if (Object.keys(lasLU).includes(place_name))
        a(href="/visualisations/censusareachanges/"+lasLU[place_name]) #[+value(place_name)]
        a
        - recordSaid(place_name)
    else 
        | !{place_name}


mixin standfirst
    - console.log("standfirst")
    //-standfirst
    - let popchange = data.population.value['change'].Population
    if (figs(data['population']['value']['2011']['Population'], 2)[1] == figs(data['population']['value']['2021']['Population'], 2)[1])
        | The size of !{place.name}'s population remained relatively unchanged
    else
        | !{place.name}'s population !{(popchange>0)? "increased":"decreased"} by around #[+nearest00(popchange)]
    | #[+tenYearsSF].
    | This semi-automated article 
    | highlights some of the most notable changes among the local population.

mixin population_heading(i)
    - console.log('population_heading')
    //-population_heading
    - var printNum = Number.parseFloat(Number.parseFloat(local_2021).toPrecision(2))
    if ((local_change/local_2011) < -0.002)
        | !{place.name+"'s"} population decreased
    else if (Math.abs(local_change/local_2011) < 0.008)
        - recordSaid('remained')
        if (local_change > 50)
            | The population grew very little
        else
            | Population size remained stable
    else if ((local_2011<1000000)&(local_2021>1000000))
        | The population passed one million
    else if ((local_2011<500000)&(local_2021>500000))
        | The population passed half a million
    else if ( (local_2011<250000) & (local_2021>250000) )
        | The population passed a quarter of a million
    else if ((local_2011<200000)&(local_2021>200000))
        | The population passed #[+value(200000)]
    else if ((local_2011<100000)&(local_2021>100000))
        | The population passed #[+value(100000)]
    else if ((local_2011<50000)&(local_2021>50000))
        | The population passed #[+value(50000)]
    else if ([250000, 500000, 1000000].includes(Number.parseFloat(Number.parseFloat(local_2021).toPrecision(2))))
        | The population
        if (get_word(local_2021, "num")[0]=="just under")
            | reached nearly 
        else
            | passed
        | #[+value(get_word(local_2021, "num")[1])]
    else
        | The population
        if ((local_2011<printNum)&(local_2021<printNum))
            | reached nearly
            |  #[+value(printNum)]
        else if ((local_2011<printNum)&(local_2021>printNum))
            | passed
            |  #[+value(printNum)]
        else if ((local_2011<printNum)&(local_2021==printNum))
            | reached
            |  #[+value(printNum)]
        else 
            | increased

mixin sent1pop(i)
    - console.log("sent1pop")
    //-sent1pop
    | #[+sentopening],
    | the population
    | of #[+value(place.name)]
    if (figs(local_2011, 2)[1] == figs(local_2021, 2)[1])
        | remained at #[+value(figs(local_2021, 2)[1])].
    else
        | #[+value(ud(local_change, 'increased by', 'fell by'))]
        if ((percent_change<0.01)&(percent_change>0))
            | just
        | #[+pc(Math.abs( percent_change*100 ))],
        | from #[+value(figs(local_2011, 2)[0])]
        | #[+value(figs(local_2011, 2)[1])] in 2011
        | to around
        | #[+value(figs(local_2021, 2)[1])] in 2021.


mixin behindPop(i, loc)
    - let this_rank = (loc=='_local') ? regional_rank_change : national_rank_change
    - let topRanks = data[s[i][0]]['value_rank'+loc]['top_bottom_change_p'][s[i][3]].filter( e => e['rank'] == 1)
    - let secRanks = data[s[i][0]]['value_rank'+loc]['top_bottom_change_p'][s[i][3]].filter( e => e['rank'] == 2)
    - console.log("behindPop", topRanks)
    | #[+placeLink(topRanks[0]['name'])]
    | (where the population increased by #[+pc(Math.abs( topRanks[0]['change_p'] ))])
    if (this_rank > 2)
        | and 
        if (topRanks.length > 1)
            | #[+placeLink(topRanks[1]['name'])]
            | (#[+pc(Math.abs( topRanks[1]['change_p'] ))])
        else
            | #[+placeLink(secRanks[0]['name'])]
            | (#[+pc(Math.abs( secRanks[0]['change_p'] ))])

mixin sent2popEngland(i)
    - console.log("sent2popEngland")
    //-sent2popEngland
    - var regComp = ( Math.round(percent_change*100) == Math.round(regional_percent_change*100) ) ? 'at a similar rate to' : ( Math.round(percent_change*100) > Math.round(regional_percent_change*100) ) ? 'by a greater percentage than' : 'by a smaller percentage than'
    - var couComp = ( Math.round(percent_change*100) == Math.round(national_percent_change*100) ) ? 'at a similar rate to' : ( Math.round(percent_change*100) > Math.round(national_percent_change*100) ) ? 'by a greater percentage than' : 'by a smaller percentage than'
    - var regDecreaseCount = region_down[rgn.name]
    - console.log("region_down", region_down)
    if (figs(local_2011, 2)[1] != figs(local_2021, 2)[1])
        if (local_change<0)
            | This
            if (regDecreaseCount==1)
                | means !{place.name} was the only local authority area
            else
                | means !{place.name} was one of 
                if (regDecreaseCount<5)
                    | only 
                | #[+value(regDecreaseCount, {'TEXTUAL':true } )] local authority areas
            | in !{parent} to see its population decline. 
            | The regional population increased by #[+value( Math.abs(regional_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})]
            | , while the population of !{country} increased by #[+value( Math.abs(national_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})].
        else
            if (( national_rank_change > 0 ) & ( national_rank_change < 4 ))
                | This means !{place.name}'s population
                | saw the
                | #[+value(ud(national_rank_change, ord(national_rank_change) + "largest", ord(national_rank_change) + "smallest"))] percentage increase
                | in !{country}
                if (national_rank_change != 1)
                    | , behind #[+behindPop(i, '')]
                | .
                | The population of !{parent} #[+value( (regional_percent_change>0)?'increased':'decreased')]
                | by #[+value( Math.abs(regional_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})],
                | while the population of !{country} #[+value( (national_percent_change>0)?'rose':'fell')]
                | by #[+value( Math.abs(national_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})].
            else if (( regional_rank_change > 0 ) & ( regional_rank_change < 4 ))
                | This means !{place.name}'s population
                | saw the
                | #[+value(ud(regional_rank_change, ord(regional_rank_change) + "largest", ord(regional_rank_change) + "smallest"))] percentage increase
                | in !{parent}
                if (regional_rank_change != 1)
                    | , behind #[+behindPop(i, '_local')]
                | .
                | The population of !{parent} #[+value( (regional_percent_change>0)?'increased':'decreased')]
                | by #[+value( Math.abs(regional_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})],
                | while the population of !{country} #[+value( (national_percent_change>0)?'rose':'fell')]
                | by #[+value( Math.abs(national_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})].
            else
                | The population here increased
                | #[+value( regComp )] 
                | the overall population of !{parent} (#[+value( Math.abs(regional_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})]), !{ (regComp == couComp)? 'and' : 'but'}
                | #[+value( couComp )] 
                | the overall population of !{cou.name} 
                | (up #[+value( Math.abs(national_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})] since the 2011 Census).

mixin sent2popWales(i)
    - console.log("sent2popWales")
    //-sent2popWales
    - var couComp = ( Math.round(percent_change*100) == Math.round(national_percent_change*100) ) ? 'at a similar rate to' : ( Math.round(percent_change*100) > Math.round(national_percent_change*100) ) ? 'by a greater percentage than' : 'by a smaller percentage than'
    - var regDecreaseCount = region_down[rgn.name]
    if (figs(local_2011, 2)[1] != figs(local_2021, 2)[1])
        if (local_change<0)
            //-  If local pop is falling and regional is rising
            | This
            if (regDecreaseCount==1)
                | means !{place.name} was the only local authority area
            else
                | means !{place.name} was one of 
                if (regDecreaseCount<5)
                    | only 
                | #[+value(regDecreaseCount, {'TEXTUAL':true } )] local authority areas
            | in !{parent} to see its population decline. 
        else
            //-  if local pop is rising and regional is rising
            | This means !{place.name}'s population 
            if (( regional_rank_change > 0 ) & ( regional_rank_change < 4 ))
                | saw the
                | #[+value(ud(regional_rank_change, ord(regional_rank_change) + "greatest increase", ord(regional_rank_change) + "smallest increase"))]
                | in Wales
                if (regional_rank_change != 1)
                    | , behind #[+behindPop(i, '_local')]
                | .
            else
                | increased
                | #[+value( couComp )] 
                | the overall population of Wales.
    | The population of Wales increased by #[+value( Math.abs(regional_percent_change), {'FORMAT': '0.0%'})]
    | , from #[+value(figs(rgn.data.population.value[2011].Population, 3)[1])]
    | to #[+value(figs(rgn.data.population.value[2021].Population, 3)[1])].

mixin sent2pop(i)
    - console.log("sent2pop")
    //-sent2pop
    if (place.parent.name == "Wales")
        | #[+sent2popWales(i)]
    else 
        | #[+sent2popEngland(i)]

mixin densRank(rank, loc)
    if Math.abs(rank>3)
        | #[+value(ord_nd( rank ))]
        | #[+value( ((rank>0)?'most':'least') )] densely
    else 
        - let dens_tb = data['density']['value_rank'+loc]['top_bottom']['Persons per football pitch']
        - let dens_samerank = dens_tb.filter( e => e['rank'] == rank)
        | #[+value((dens_samerank.length>1)?'joint ':'')]
        | #[+value(ud(rank, ord(rank) + "most", ord(rank) + "least"))] densely

mixin behindDens(rank, loc)
    - let dens_tb = data['density']['value_rank'+loc]['top_bottom']['Persons per football pitch']
    - let rl = data['density']['value_rank'+loc]['2021']['Persons per football pitch']
    - var topranks_3 = dens_tb.filter( e=> (rl<0)? (e['rank'] == -1) : (e['rank'] == 1) )
    - var secranks_3 = dens_tb.filter( e=> (rl<0)? (e['rank'] == -2) : (e['rank'] == 2) )
    | #[+placeLink(topranks_3[0]['name'])]
    | #[+county(topranks_3[0]['name'])]
    - console.log("bD", rank)
    if (Math.abs(rank)==3)
        - console.log("behindDens")
        if (topranks_3.length == 1)
            | and 
            | #[+placeLink(secranks_3[0]['name'])]
            | #[+county(secranks_3[0]['name'])]
        else
            | and 
            | #[+placeLink(topranks_3[1]['name'])]
            | #[+county(topranks_3[1]['name'])]

mixin density 
    - console.log("density")
    - let density_rank_21 = data['density']['value_rank']['2021']['Persons per football pitch']
    - let density_loc_rank_21 = data['density']['value_rank_local']['2021']['Persons per football pitch']
    //-density
    if (rgn.name=='Wales')
        - country = 'Wales'
    - let ppfp2 = Math.round(data.density.value[2011]['Persons per football pitch'] * 10)/10
    - let ppfp = Math.round(data.density.value[2021]['Persons per football pitch'] * 10)/10
    if (ppfp==ppfp2)
        | In 2021, #[+value(place.name)] was home to around #[+value(ppfp)] #[+value(pluralize('person', ppfp))] per football pitch-sized piece of land.
    else
        | In 2021, #[+value(place.name)] was home to around 
        | #[+value(ppfp, {'FORMAT': "0.0"})] #[+value(pluralize('person', ppfp))]
        | per football pitch-sized piece of land, compared with 
        | #[+value(ppfp2, {'FORMAT': "0.0"})] in 2011.
    if (country == 'Wales')
        | This area was the 
        | #[+densRank(density_rank_21, "")]
        | populated out of all 22 local authority areas across Wales 
        if ([2,3,-2,-3].includes(density_rank_21))
            | (after #[+behindDens(density_rank_21, '')])
        | .
    else
        if (Math.abs(density_rank_21) < 4)
            | This area was the
            | #[+densRank(density_rank_21, "")] populated
            | local authority area across England
            if (Math.abs(density_rank_21)!=1)
                | (after #[+behindDens(density_rank_21, '')])
            | .
        else if (Math.abs(density_loc_rank_21) < 4)
            | This area was the 
            | #[+densRank(density_loc_rank_21, "_local")] 
            | populated local authority area across !{parent}
            if (Math.abs(density_loc_rank_21)!=1)
                | (after #[+behindDens(density_loc_rank_21, '_local')])
            | .
        else
            if ((Math.abs(get_percent(density_rank_21)) == 50)|((Math.abs(get_percent(density_rank_21)) == 55)))
                | This area was close to the median population density across English local authority areas at the last census.
            else if (get_percent(density_rank_21)>0)
                | This area was among the top
                | #[+pcr(Math.abs(get_percent(density_rank_21)))]
                | most densely populated English local authority areas 
                | at the last census.
            else
                | This area was among the lowest
                | #[+pcr(Math.abs(get_percent(density_rank_21)))]
                | for population density across English local authority areas
                | at the last census.

mixin subheadAge(i)
    - console.log("subheadAge")
    //-subheadAge
    if (Math.abs(local_change) == 1)
        | Median age #[+value(place.preposition)] #[+value(place.name)]
    else if ((local_change>1)&(local_2021<regional_2021))
        | Median age increased
    else if ((local_change<-1)&(local_2021>regional_2021))
        | Median age decreased
    else if (local_2011 != local_2021)
        | #[+value(ud(local_change, 'An older ', 'A younger ') + place.nameNoThe )]
    else 
        | Median age stable #[+value(place.preposition)] #[+value(place.name)]

mixin sent1Age(i)
    - console.log("sent1Age")
    //-sent1Age
    if (local_2011 != local_2021)
        p
            | Between the last two censuses, the average (median) age
            | of #[+value(place.name)] 
            if (local_2011 == local_2021)
                | remained
            else
                | #[+value(ud(local_change, 'increased by', 'decreased by'))]
                | #[+value(Math.abs(local_change), {'TEXTUAL':true })] 
                | #[+value(Math.abs(local_change)==1?'year':'years')],
                | from #[+value(local_2011)] to
            | #[+value(local_2021)] years of age.
    else 
        p
            | The latest census data also show that the average (median) age remained #[+value(local_2021)] years #[+value(place.preposition)] #[+value(place.name)] 
            | between the last two censuses.


mixin sent2Age(i)
    - console.log("sent2Age")
    //-sent2Age
    - let agediff = local_2021-national_2021
    - let agediff01 = local_2011-national_2011
    if (country=="England")
        | This area had 
        if (Math.abs(national_rank_2021)==1)
            | the #[+value((national_rank_2021>0)?'highest':'lowest')] average (median) age of any local authority area in England.
            | Across the country, the overall average (median) age was #[+value(national_2021)] years of age in 2021.
        else
            if (Math.abs(regional_rank_2021)<3)
                | the #[+value(jointrank(regional_rank_2021, s[i], "_local", place, "")[0])] 
                | #[+value(ud(regional_rank_2021, ord(regional_rank_2021) + "highest", ord(regional_rank_2021) + "lowest"))]
                | average (median) age in #[+value(parent)] 
                | #[+alongside_age(jointrank(regional_rank_2021, s[i], "_local", place, ""), regional_rank_2021)]
                | and 
            else
                | a 
                if (local_2021==regional_2021)
                    | similar average (median) age to
                else
                    | #[+value(adv(local_2021, regional_2021))] 
                    | #[+value(ud(local_2021-regional_2021, 'higher', 'lower'))]
                    | average (median) age than 
                | #[+value(parent)] as a whole in 2021 (#[+value(regional_2021)] years) 
                | #[+value((Math.sign(agediff) == Math.sign(local_2021-regional_2021)?'and':'but'))]
            if (local_2021==national_2021)
                | had a similar averaage (median) age to England (#[+value(national_2021)] years).
            else
                | a
                | #[+value(Math.abs(agediff)<2?'slightly': '')] 
                | #[+value(ud(agediff, 'higher', 'lower'))] 
                | average (median) age than England (#[+value(national_2021)] years).
    else
        | This area had
        | a #[+value(adv(local_2021, near_2021))] 
        | #[+value(ud(local_2021-near_2021, 'higher', 'lower'))]
        | average (median) age than nearby #[+placeLink(near.name)] (#[+value(near_2021)] years) and
        if (Math.abs(regional_rank_2021)<3)
            | the 
            | #[+value(jointrank(regional_rank_2021, s[i], "", place, "")[0])] 
            | #[+value(ud(regional_rank_2021, ord(regional_rank_2021) + "highest", ord(regional_rank_2021) + "lowest"))]
            | average (median) age in #[+value(parent)]
            | #[+alongside_age(jointrank(regional_rank_2021, s[i], "_local", place, ""), regional_rank_2021)]
            | .
        else if (local_2021==regional_2021)
            | had a similar average (median) age to Wales as a whole (#[+value(regional_2021)] years).
        else
            | a
            | #[+value(Math.abs(agediff)<2?'slightly':'')] 
            | #[+value(ud(agediff, 'higher', 'lower'))] 
            | average (median) age than Wales as a whole (#[+value(regional_2021)] years).
        | #[+small_disclaimer(place.near.name)]
    p
        | The median age is the age of the person in the middle of the group, meaning that one half of the group is younger than that person and the other half is older.

